Initial values:
x = outer-x
y = outer-y

Calling function with parameter:

Inside function (parameter shadows outer x):
x = parameter-value (should be parameter value, not outer x)
y = outer-y (should be outer-y)
After modifying parameter:
x = modified-parameter (should be modified-parameter)

After function call:
x = outer-x (should still be outer-x)
y = outer-y (should still be outer-y)

Calling outer function:

In outer function:
a = outer-parameter-value (parameter value)
x = outer-x (outer scope x)

In inner function:
a = outer-parameter-value (from outer function)
x = inner-parameter-value (parameter value, shadows outer x)
After modifying inner parameter:
x = modified-inner-parameter

After inner function call:
x = outer-x (should still be outer-x, not modified)

Final outer scope values:
x = outer-x (should still be outer-x)
y = outer-y (should still be outer-y)

Test completed successfully!
